cy":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.08593343807259901,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":5.6,"_gate_rev_durability":0.04038291235750391,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":45.2,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.09420304812653149,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.005106487936058501,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":43.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.022890678272030805,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":61.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.022249999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":14.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Artisan Partners Asset Management Inc. is publicly owned investment manager. It provides its services to pension and profit sharing plans, trusts, endowments, foundations, charitable organizations, government entities, private funds and non-U.S. funds, as well as mutual funds, non-U.S. funds and collective trusts. It manages separate client-focused equity and fixed income portfolios. The firm invests in the public equity and fixed income markets across the globe. It invests in growth and value stocks of companies across all market capitalization. For fixed income component of its portfolio the firm invests in non-investment grade corporate bonds and secured and unsecured loans. It employs fundamental analysis to create its portfolios. Artisan Partners Asset Management Inc. was founded in 1994 and is based in Milwaukee, Wisconsin with additional offices in Atlanta, Georgia; New York City; San Francisco, California; Leawood, Kansas; and London, United Kingdom.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jason A. Gottlieb | CEO, Director & President | Age 55 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 567 people. Revenue per employee of $2.1M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $303K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $48K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Artisan Partners Asset Manageme is a mid-cap financial services business with a $2.7B market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +6.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 63% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 53-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $172M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.59\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 47\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 9.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +7.5% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 39% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Artisan Partners Asset Management (NYSE:APAM) Stock Rating Upgraded by Zacks Research","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/artisan-partners-asset-management-nyseapam-stock-rating-upgraded-by-zacks-research.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794571243.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"AUM Update Might Change The Case For Investing In Artisan Partners (APAM)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-apam/artisan-partners-asset-management/news/aum-update-might-change-the-case-for-investing-in-artisan-pa","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794526217.706,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.866,"tier":0